{
  "area": "bvi",
  "method": "British Virgin Islands: Tortola and its outer cays, Peter, Norman, Salt, Cooper and Ginger Islands, the Dog Islands, Virgin Gorda, Scrub Island, Great Camanoe and Guana Island, and the offshore Chikuzen; Anegada is included in scope but no resident operator publishes Anegada sites, so none is counted. Lists used: five independent operator lists (Dive BVI, whose Willy T page is read with its site list; Sail Caribbean Divers; Blue Water Divers; Sunchaser Scuba; and the Cuan Law liveaboard's list of 'a small selection of the 100 plus sites'). The BVI National Parks Trust runs the Halas mooring buoy system (white buoys are dive-only) but publishes no named mooring list; its marine page and an archived mooring page were read and name no sites, and the Rhone is a National Park marine site by Trust description only. The BVI Tourist Board diving page and bvi-dive-map.com (a web agency's directory) name no sites and are not counted. A site is counted when named on at least two independent lists and recreationally divable. Dive BVI's combined 'Coral Gardens / Sharkplaneo' and 'Visibles / POS' are one row each, as are the two Brewers Bay pinnacle dives; same-named sites on different islands (Shark Point off Scrub Island versus off Peter Island) are separate rows. The Indians, Baths and Caves snorkel entries on Sail Caribbean's list are snorkel-only and kept as excluded except The Indians, which Blue Water and Cuan Law also list as a scuba site. No list gives coordinates. Counted 2026-10-14.",
